# Changelog

## Unreleased

### Added

- Presets for glow, harlequin and helix, each recorded end to end in an empty sandbox. Their steps and waits come from `anina init`; harlequin and helix check their result inside the tape (`Wait "27,211"`, `Exec grep`).
- `anina audit --preset NAME [--part P]`: a preset's parts played in every terminal of the matrix, each one starting from the sandbox as prepare left it. Between terminals only what a play changed is put back, permissions and edits that kept size and mtime included, with the times it had, so a build in the next terminal is not redone (ADR-0016).
- `anina compare A B`: two runs compared with timing taken out (files, screens as text, PNG pixels, reports). From a report it leaves out the clock, the durations and the latencies (an exploration's `latency_ms` too), so two audits of the same program match. Measures taken over the screens a run happened to sample (colored and visible cells, contrast, the screenshot each terminal keeps, volatile cells) are shown side by side, not judged. Their verdicts still are: the readability score within 5 points, and whether each terminal kept to its colors (`colors_respected` in the report). Exits 1 on a difference.
- `--embed` on `run` and `audit`: the images go inside `index.html` / `report.html`, one file to share.
- Every PNG anina writes carries the text of the screen it shows, and `anina check` reads it. `run`, `record`, `audit` and `explore` end with that check on the files they wrote, whether they worked or failed (a failed wait leaves `failed.txt`), judged by ctime, so a copy that kept its mtime (`cp -p`, `rsync -a`, `tar x`, `mv`) is checked too. A note kept in the output folder, or what an earlier run left there, is for `anina check` to read.
- A tape warns when a `Type` with several words ends in something that reads as a delay: it is typed as text; `Type@30ms` sets the delay.
- `SECURITY.md`: what redaction and the sandbox hold, by mode and by system, what neither does, and how to report a problem. The README's Privacy section follows it.
- `tool/tasks/selfcheck.sh`: anina on its own output. It plays the `shell` preset and runs `anina compare` against the run kept in `tool/tests/shell/` for the system (macOS or Linux), so a change in what anina records fails, with the files that differ and a diff of each text. `--update` records the reference again; a change that is meant brings it in the same pull request (ADR-0017).

### Fixed

- `--sandbox strict` holds for everything a run starts. A tape's `Exec`, a preset's `[[prepare]]` and `explore --before` now run inside the OS sandbox, behind the same prefix as the program; before, only the program did, and the shell lines of the same run wrote wherever they could. A refused line fails with the reason: `the sandbox refused it: --sandbox strict allows writes only under the sandbox root (...)`. `prepare` may also write anina's cache, where presets keep clones and builds; a toolchain's own cache (`~/.cargo`) is not writable, so a build that fills one runs first under `env` (ADR-0006).
- Under `--sandbox strict` on macOS, a program can no longer remove the sandbox root and leave a link in its place, and a root that is a link is refused.
- A run stops when a `prepare` moved a folder that holds the sandbox root, or left a link on the way to the root or to its saved copy: `prepare moved the sandbox root or put a link in its path`. Before, anina followed the link and made or removed folders where it pointed. The next run checks the way to its root before it empties it, and on macOS `strict` refuses the move itself.
- A built-in preset is no longer emptied and extracted through a link left at `presets` in anina's cache, where a `prepare` can write: the run stops with `a symbolic link or the name leads elsewhere`. Before, the folder of the preset's name on the other side of the link was removed and filled.
- On macOS, recordings no longer show the per-user temp folder (`/var/folders/<id>/T`): status lines print it as `$TMPDIR/...`, redaction hides it on screen as `$TMPDIR` (`temp path`), and `anina check` reports it. The shared `/tmp` stays as it is.
- Redaction no longer pulls a row of output up into the line above it. A row that fills the width and is followed by text looked wrapped, so hiding a path in it laid the next row onto its end (`ab ~/xyzwhello`) and a `Wait` on that output failed. A match inside one row is now replaced in that row; a match the wrap cuts is still hidden across both.
- On macOS, `bash` tapes no longer open with the notice that the default shell is now zsh: every program gets `BASH_SILENCE_DEPRECATION_WARNING=1` unless the tape sets it.

- Status lines no longer print the machine's paths: a path shows relative to the working directory, or as `~/...`, also when anina runs from `/` or from above HOME. The audit summary printed the full tape path.
- `anina init` writes waits that hold in the other sizes `anina audit` tries. Text new to the session comes first (a closing popup that uncovers old text does not count); after typing, the wait is the end of what was typed and then what the program did with it (new text away from the echo, `Gone` for rows a filter took away); after a scroll, new text within half the smallest terminal's height of the cursor, counted as rows wrap at 60 columns, and `Idle 3` only when there is none; a wait is picked the way the replay matches it and is never cut at a wrap edge (ADR-0015); a wait or a `Gone` is at most 24 characters, ends before column 56 (counted in columns: a wide character takes two) and is never a padded row or a counter. The echo ends at the cursor: a cursor that jumped to a field (`/` in less) doesn't turn the screen into echo. Text keys under 0.25 s apart stay one `Type` even when a completion popup redraws the screen, except a `/` or `:` that opened a field: it is a step of its own, with its wait.
- `tool/tasks/fullcheck.sh` packages under a new target path on every run. Cargo unpacks packaged crates by the registry's path and never again at the same version, so a reused path, even emptied, verified the workspace against crates an earlier run had packaged. On its way out it removes those unpacked copies. Packaging and that cleanup run under a lock shared by every worktree, so one fullcheck never removes the copy another is building against.
- A literal `Wait` matches text the terminal wrapped at its edge: a typed line longer than 60 columns no longer fails its wait in the 60x20 audit terminal.
- A preset's sandbox with a socket, a FIFO or a read-only folder (Go's module cache) no longer breaks `audit --preset`, and a second `anina run` can empty it. Each sandbox keeps its saved copy under `pristine/<name>` in the cache: two presets whose names differ after a dot no longer share one.
- A wrong `--part` fails before the sandbox is emptied and prepare runs; it used to fail after a clone and a release build. A preset is looked up once per run, so a built-in one is extracted once.
- `anina presets` no longer lists a folder in `demo/` without a `preset.toml` as an invalid built-in preset, and `anina run` refuses it by name.
- The `journey.tape` that `anina audit -- PROGRAM` keeps reads back as the command that ran. A word with `$` or a leading `~` (`sh -c 'echo $HOME'`) was written between double quotes, where the tape language expands it: played again, the tape ran another command, or stopped on a variable nobody set. Such words now go between single quotes.
- `anina init` no longer takes a terminal's cursor position report (`ESC [ 12 ; 40 R`) for F3 with modifiers. It read as `ctrl+alt+shift+f3` unless the column was 1, 17, 33 and so on; now only `ESC [ 1 ; modifier R` is the key, and a report is noted in the tape as input no step can say.
- `anina audit` lists the color pairs that fail contrast in the same order on every run. A pair that failed both as text and as a graphic came out in either order.

### Changed

- CI (`gatecheck`) runs `tool/tasks/fullcheck.sh` itself, so a developer and CI pass the same gates from one list: fmt, clippy, test, doctor, selfcheck, deny, package. `cargo deny check` and the self-check are new in CI. Beside it stand `cargo check` on Rust 1.90 (the `rust-version` of the manifest), the release build, and a coverage summary on each run. The workflow's token only reads the repository, and every action is pinned by commit.
- Under `--sandbox strict` the network is off unless the preset says `network = true`, the loopback included. The field was only printed by `anina presets`. `explore --sandbox strict` has no preset and so no network. The presets that need it (`astro`, `burn`, `urna`) already declare it.
- The run's part line reads `part 1/1 edit · title` (a middle dot instead of a dash), so the output pastes into docs as is.
- One crate became a workspace of five under `rust/` (ADR-0013): `anina-screen`, `anina-runner`, `anina-render`, `anina-record` and the `anina` binary. Commands, flags and output are the same. The split first carried four more crates with no code (`anina-codecs`, `anina-design`, `anina-motion`, `anina-recode`); they are gone, and a crate comes back the day its first line is written.
- Modules renamed on the way:
  - `ansi`, `cast`, `teach` -> `anina_screen::escape`, `frames`, `lesson`
  - `engine::tuitest`, `engine::tmux` -> `anina_runner::engine::tuitest`, `tmux`, names kept
  - `tape`, `volatile`, `privacy` -> `anina_runner::script`, `masker`, `redact`
  - `render::font`, `gallery` -> `anina_render::fonts`, `index`; `render::png`, `svg` and `brand` -> `anina_render::png`, `svg` and `brand`, names kept
  - `record` -> `anina_record`; `sandbox` (`fsdiff`) -> `anina_record::cordon` (`diffs`); `preset::manifest`, `report` -> `anina_record::preset::specs`, `print`
  - `audit` (`contrast`, `matrix`, `measure`, `report`) -> `audits` (`ratio`, `cases`, `meter`, `print`)
  - `explore` -> `mapper`; `init` (`keys`, `passthrough`, `tapegen`) -> `taping` (`input`, `relay`, `print`); `check` -> `checks`
- A module that holds one thing the world already named keeps that name, whatever its length: an engine, a file format, an operating system (ADR-0010). The engines and the SVG and PNG writers were `inner`, `outer`, `shape` and `pixel` for seven weeks of this cycle and are `tuitest`, `tmux`, `svg` and `png` again. Every other module keeps the name the split gave it.
- `presets/` is `demo/`. The CI workflow is `gatecheck.yml`.
- The folders that held only a `.gitkeep` are gone: seven under `demo/` (presets still to come) and `pkgs/` with its four. Every folder in `demo/` is a preset.
- Releases are tagged `v{{version}}` for the whole workspace.
